# Independently reviewed native stop fixture

This is a lead-operated non-managed fixture, not task50 producer code. It owns
no Kata issue, worker seat or native goal, and cannot accept a milestone.
All runtime effects wait for an immutable source commit, cold retention,
independent source review and explicit `NativeFixtureLaunchAdmission`.

`native_stop_fixture.py launch --authorization ABS --authorization-sha256 HEX
--output ABS` runs inside an explicitly admitted exclusive cgroup with at most
256 MiB RAM and zero swap. The admission pins source bytes, candidate, independent
reviewer thread, retention, user authority, socket/peer/daemon incarnation,
operator scope, separate fixture workspace/common Git directory and fresh output.
The fixed command digest pins its own immutable payload source and owned output.
Launch reopens actual Git facts from a clean linked worktree on the unique
`codex/collaboration50-fixture/<fixture-id>` branch at the admitted base,
checks directory incarnations and rejects canonical/source/output overlap.
Git, Python and systemd-run use absolute digest-pinned executables; payload Python
uses isolated mode. Each Upgrade/request/frame has a whole-operation deadline,
so a peer dribbling bytes cannot extend a request beyond its admitted timeout.

Only `thread/start` and `thread/shellCommand` mutate native state. The former
creates one fresh no-goal thread with `approvalPolicy=never`, explicit
`danger-full-access` and cooperative workspace roots. The latter sends one fixed
command with a 40-second native timeout. The command creates a separate 128 MiB,
zero-swap scope; its single Python payload records an actual live process and
cgroup witness, waits 15 seconds and returns. No subprocess, Git/source/scientific
write, model turn or daemon stop is part of the payload. Native shell commands
are explicitly unsandboxed; they do not prove model-worker permission grants.
The operator keeps its connection for another 45 seconds. Every request is
durable before send, raw matching responses are retained, unrelated/private
notifications are discarded, and uncertainty never licenses a mutation retry.

The shell RPC acknowledgement contains no returned turn ID. The independently
admitted A50 observer must derive the actual fresh turn/item/handle identity from
complete native lists and match the literal command digest and live process
witness. `fixture-launch.json` is raw provenance, not a stop receipt. Neither
the acknowledgement nor `operator-returning.json` proves terminal tools, empty
queue, quiescence, cleanup or retirement. Missing native association/coverage is
a retained blocker; no invented `turn/start` receipt or scan-only fallback exists.

Separate model-worker/common-Git/nested-Insula capability and isolated Kata
proofs remain required before task50 producer implementation/managed effects.
Changing transport framing preserves the full original stop/queue/tool/process
contract, independent Insula gates, budgets and historical authorization pins.
